    "notes": "A split hero pairs a left-aligned white promo card — eyebrow badges, a large serif headline, a supporting line, and two side-by-side CTA buttons — with a full-bleed lifestyle photo filling the rest of the banner. Below it, a four-column row of circular icon badges with bold labels and short subtext communicates trust signals in a compact, scannable strip. A centered section heading introduces a three-column product grid, where each card shows a square product photo, small corner badges, a title, price, and a review-count link. Further down, a row of photo tiles with a caption and arrow link functions as a visual category-navigation system, and the page closes with a row of star-rated testimonial cards showing quoted feedback and a reviewer name/date. This pattern would suit a direct-to-consumer product or grooming brand aiming for a premium, editorial storefront feel.",
    "promptFragment": "[site]\nBuild a multi-section ecommerce landing page with a warm neutral background, serif display type for headlines paired with a clean sans-serif for UI/body text, and consistent card corner-radius and spacing across all sections. Section order top to bottom: hero, trust badges, product grid, category tiles, testimonials. Customization options: color palette (neutral/earth tones, monochrome, or brand-accent), overall spacing density (compact vs. spacious), and typography pairing (serif+sans vs. all-sans).\n\n[hero]\nBuild a split hero banner: a white promo card anchored left containing small eyebrow badges/labels, a large serif headline (2-3 lines), a short supporting line, an oversized stat/number callout with underline accent, and two side-by-side CTA buttons (one solid dark, one outlined) — positioned next to a full-bleed lifestyle photo filling the remaining hero width. Customization options: number of CTAs (1 or 2), card position (left/right), presence of stat callout, and image treatment (full color, cropped, duotone).\n\n[trust badges]\nBuild a four-column row of trust-badge cards, each with a centered circular icon, a bold short label beneath it, and a one-line description in smaller muted text. Customization options: badge count (3–5), icon style (line vs. filled), and card background (flat color, subtle border, or none).\n\n[cards]\nBuild a three-column product card grid with a centered section heading above it. Each card shows a square product image with a small corner badge (top-left) and an optional circular tag badge (top-right), followed by a product title, price, and a small review-count indicator with a star/icon. Customization options: grid columns (2–4), badge presence/count, price formatting, and hover state (image zoom, shadow lift, or none).\n\n[category tiles]\nBuild a row of photo tiles functioning as category navigation, each showing a full-bleed photo with a caption label and arrow icon overlaid at the bottom edge. Customization options: tile count, aspect ratio (square vs. portrait), and caption style (overlay bar vs. floating text).\n\n[testimonials]\nBuild a row of testimonial cards, each with a star rating row at the top, a short quoted review in body text, and a reviewer name with date beneath it. Customization options: layout (static row vs. carousel), card count visible at once, and inclusion of reviewer avatar.",
